{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Real-Time Vision \u2014 Edge Deployment Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Measure latency correctly"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import time"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def measure_latency(model, input_shape, device=\"cpu\", warmup=10, iters=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = model.to(device).eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = torch.randn(input_shape, device=device)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(warmup):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            model(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if device == \"cuda\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            torch.cuda.synchronize()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        times = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(iters):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if device == \"cuda\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                torch.cuda.synchronize()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            t0 = time.perf_counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            model(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if device == \"cuda\":"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                torch.cuda.synchronize()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            times.append((time.perf_counter() - t0) * 1000)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    times.sort()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return {"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"p50_ms\": times[len(times) // 2],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"p95_ms\": times[int(len(times) * 0.95)],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"p99_ms\": times[int(len(times) * 0.99)],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        \"mean_ms\": sum(times) / len(times),"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Warm up, synchronise, use `time.perf_counter()`. Report percentiles, not just mean."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Parameter and FLOP counts"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def parameter_count(model):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return sum(p.numel() for p in model.parameters())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def flops_estimate(model, input_shape):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Rough FLOP count for a conv/linear-only model. For production use `fvcore` or `ptflops`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    \"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    total = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def conv_hook(m, inp, out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nonlocal total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        c_out, c_in, kh, kw = m.weight.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h, w = out.shape[-2:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += 2 * c_in * c_out * kh * kw * h * w"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def linear_hook(m, inp, out):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        nonlocal total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total += 2 * m.in_features * m.out_features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hooks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for m in model.modules():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if isinstance(m, torch.nn.Conv2d):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            hooks.append(m.register_forward_hook(conv_hook))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        elif isinstance(m, torch.nn.Linear):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            hooks.append(m.register_forward_hook(linear_hook))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model(torch.randn(input_shape))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for h in hooks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        h.remove()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return total"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "For real projects use `fvcore.nn.FlopCountAnalysis` or `ptflops`; they handle every module type correctly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Post-training static quantisation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def quantise_ptq(model, calibration_loader, backend=\"x86\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    import torch.ao.quantization as tq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = model.eval().cpu()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model.qconfig = tq.get_default_qconfig(backend)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tq.prepare(model, inplace=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    with torch.no_grad():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for x, _ in calibration_loader:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            model(x)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    tq.convert(model, inplace=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return model"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three steps: configure, prepare (insert observers), calibrate with real data, convert (fuse + quantise). Requires the model to be fused (`Conv -> BN -> ReLU` -> `ConvBnReLU`), which `torch.ao.quantization.fuse_modules` handles."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Export to ONNX"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def export_onnx(model, sample_input, path=\"model.onnx\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = model.eval()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    torch.onnx.export("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        model,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sample_input,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        path,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        input_names=[\"input\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        output_names=[\"output\"],"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        dynamic_axes={\"input\": {0: \"batch\"}, \"output\": {0: \"batch\"}},"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        opset_version=17,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "`opset_version=17` is the safe default in 2026. `dynamic_axes` lets you run the ONNX model with arbitrary batch size."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: Benchmark and compare regimes"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import torch.nn as nn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from torchvision.models import mobilenet_v3_small"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def compare_regimes():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model = mobilenet_v3_small(weights=None, num_classes=10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    params = parameter_count(model)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    flops = flops_estimate(model, (1, 3, 224, 224))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lat_fp32 = measure_latency(model, (1, 3, 224, 224), device=\"cpu\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"FP32 MobileNetV3-Small: {params:,} params  {flops/1e9:.2f} GFLOPs  \""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "          f\"p50={lat_fp32['p50_ms']:.2f}ms  p95={lat_fp32['p95_ms']:.2f}ms\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Run the same function for `resnet50`, `efficientnet_v2_s`, and `convnext_tiny` and you have the comparison table you need for a deployment decision."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **(Easy)** Measure p50 latency for `resnet18`, `mobilenet_v3_small`, `efficientnet_v2_s`, and `convnext_tiny` at 224x224 on CPU. Report the table and identify which architecture has the best accuracy-per-ms.\n2. **(Medium)** Apply post-training static quantisation to `mobilenet_v3_small`. Report FP32 vs INT8 latency and accuracy loss on a held-out subset of CIFAR-10 or similar.\n3. **(Hard)** Export `convnext_tiny` to ONNX, run it through `onnxruntime` with the `CPUExecutionProvider`, and compare latency to the PyTorch eager baseline. Identify the first layer where ONNX Runtime is faster and explain why."
      ]
    }
